    "0.5.0": {
        "info": {
            "author": "",
            "author_email": "Nara Torres Moreira <nara.moreira@astrazeneca.com>",
            "bugtrack_url": null,
            "classifiers": [
                "License :: OSI Approved :: MIT License",
                "Operating System :: OS Independent",
                "Programming Language :: Python :: 3"
            ],
            "description": "# Optimisation Tools\n\nWelcome to opt-tools, a repository with different generic optimisation tools to be reused across different projects!\n\nThe optimisation tools currently available for use are:\n\n- `opt_framework`: an optimisation framework that provides an extensive structure for solving an optimisation problem, and aims to reduce coding time and increase standardisation across different projects. It should be imported in your optimisation project and extended with the implementation of the problem-specific classes and methods.\n- `perform_analysis`: OPA is an Optimisation Performance Analysis tool that makes it easier for developers to analyse results from their optimisation algorithms.\n- `solution_polish`: an algorithm that helps solving hard MIP or LP models.\n\nThe folder `examples` includes implementation of toy-examples of how to use opt-tools.\n\n\n## Quickstart\n\nTo get up and running, install Poetry if you haven't already, and then run the following command from the root of the repository to install all the project's dependencies into a new Python virtual environment on your machine.\n\n```shell\n$ poetry install\n```\n",
